{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"663830d4f5c60a48","name":"card_event_diplomatic_attache","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_diplomatic_attache","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DIPLOMATIC ATTACHÉ","text":"Deal 1 damage to target enemy, plus 1 for each previously played DIPLOMATIC ATTACHÉ.","flavorText":"The Tripartite Pact, signed in 1940, was a mutual defense treaty between Nazi Germany, Fascist Italy, and Imperial Japan. It aimed to establish a formal alliance and coordination among the Axis powers. The pact outlined principles of mutual assistance and collaboration in economic, political, and military matters. Germany sought support from Italy and Japan to expand the Axis alliance, Italy aimed to strengthen its position within the Axis and gain backing for its colonial ambitions, while Japan sought resources and influence in East Asia. The pact included provisions for mutual defense, consultation, and economic cooperation. However, the effectiveness of the pact was limited as each nation pursued its own strategic goals independently. While symbolically important, the pact did not lead to significant military coordination or joint planning among the signatories. Ultimately, the Tripartite Pact had a symbolic and diplomatic role, but its impact on the outcome of the war was limited as the fortunes of the Axis powers declined.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_diplomatic_attache","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_diplomatic_attache_title","SourceString":"DIPLOMATIC ATTACHÉ","LocalizedString":"DIPLOMATIC ATTACHÉ"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_diplomatic_attache_text","SourceString":"Deal 1 damage to target enemy, plus 1 for each previously played DIPLOMATIC ATTACHÉ.","LocalizedString":"Deal 1 damage to target enemy, plus 1 for each previously played DIPLOMATIC ATTACHÉ."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_diplomatic_attache_history","SourceString":"The Tripartite Pact, signed in 1940, was a mutual defense treaty between Nazi Germany, Fascist Italy, and Imperial Japan. It aimed to establish a formal alliance and coordination among the Axis powers. The pact outlined principles of mutual assistance and collaboration in economic, political, and military matters. Germany sought support from Italy and Japan to expand the Axis alliance, Italy aimed to strengthen its position within the Axis and gain backing for its colonial ambitions, while Japan sought resources and influence in East Asia. The pact included provisions for mutual defense, consultation, and economic cooperation. However, the effectiveness of the pact was limited as each nation pursued its own strategic goals independently. While symbolically important, the pact did not lead to significant military coordination or joint planning among the signatories. Ultimately, the Tripartite Pact had a symbolic and diplomatic role, but its impact on the outcome of the war was limited as the fortunes of the Axis powers declined.","LocalizedString":"The Tripartite Pact, signed in 1940, was a mutual defense treaty between Nazi Germany, Fascist Italy, and Imperial Japan. It aimed to establish a formal alliance and coordination among the Axis powers. The pact outlined principles of mutual assistance and collaboration in economic, political, and military matters. Germany sought support from Italy and Japan to expand the Axis alliance, Italy aimed to strengthen its position within the Axis and gain backing for its colonial ambitions, while Japan sought resources and influence in East Asia. The pact included provisions for mutual defense, consultation, and economic cooperation. However, the effectiveness of the pact was limited as each nation pursued its own strategic goals independently. While symbolically important, the pact did not lead to significant military coordination or joint planning among the signatories. Ultimately, the Tripartite Pact had a symbolic and diplomatic role, but its impact on the outcome of the war was limited as the fortunes of the Axis powers declined."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardCreatedAlterCard"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Spring2023Candidates/t_diplomat.t_diplomat","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Japanese WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/DIPLOMATIC_ATTACHE.DIPLOMATIC_ATTACHE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":354.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_diplomatic_attache_photo","SourceString":"Signing of the Tripartite Pact, 1940. ","LocalizedString":"Signing of the Tripartite Pact, 1940. "},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"isRemoval":true},"variables":[{"name":"count","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_diplomatic_attache_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name